es on a clean CI host, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the bead ANSI snapshot matches in every environment, and all three [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]test-matrix legs finish inside their timeout.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ci_green_restoration.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/ci_green_restoration.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-dz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-dz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Raise the published sase-core-rs floor to 0.17.8[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-floor[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-floor: bump the pyproject dependency window so the published-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]smoke lane installs a sase-core-rs release that actually exposes every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]binding this repo calls, and refresh the recorded lock specifier to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]match.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make bead prose highlighting ignore ambient NO_COLOR[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]bead-color[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead-color: force color on the internal rendering console so `--color [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]always` wins over the ambient NO_COLOR environment variable, restore the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlighted ANSI golden that was overwritten with degraded output, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add a regression test that renders under NO_COLOR.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fit the test matrix inside its job timeout[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]ci-budget[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ci-budget: raise the test job timeout and stop running coverage on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]matrix legs that never upload it, so the slowest interpreter leg can [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]finish instead of being cancelled at the limit.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Skip the prompt-archive check when its context is unavailable[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]validate-skip[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]validate-skip: teach the prompt-archive validation an explicit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unavailable-context outcome and have `sase validate` report it as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]skipped rather than failed, so a clean host without a project registry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]or agents-sidecar clone can still run the aggregate validation.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Publish the plans-sidecar prompt migration[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]publish-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]publish-migration: finish and publish the historical prompt migration so[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the plans sidecar remote no longer carries prompt Markdown or dangling [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]relative prompt links, coordinating with the in-progress phase bead that[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already owns this work instead of redoing it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Confirm a fully green master run[/bold #D7AFFF]              